  "instruction": "Model a house with basement at -3 m, ground floor at 0 m and attic at 3 m. Each storey is 8 m east-west by 6 m north-south, split into west and east rooms of 4 by 6 m with a connecting door. Ground has an exterior entrance. Add straight stairs basement-west to ground-west and ground-east to attic-east, each 4 m long, 0.8 m wide, 15 steps, clear of walls and doors. Use 150 mm walls, 200 mm slabs, 2.7 m wall height below attic, 4.2 m nominal attic walls and a 200 mm gable roof with 2.7 m eaves, 4.2 m ridge along X. Preserve history. Explain estimated construction and stair assumptions for human review.",
  "summary": "Three-storey 8 × 6 m house with six rooms, connecting doors, ground entrance, two straight stairs, slabs and gabled roof.",
  "rationale": "Reconstructs the empty original shell under explicit building scope at -3, 0 and +3 m. Reuses entrance identity and south offset. No contents need relocation. Historical revisions remain unchanged; acceptance is separate.",
  "constraints": "Wall-centreline dimensions reduce clear sizes by wall thickness. Uses specified walls, slabs and roof; roof heights are attic-relative, no overhang. Stairs ascend north at X=1.6/6 m, Y=1–5 m, away from doors, with end landing space and derived voids. Each has 4 m horizontal run, 0.8 m width, 15 steps over 3 m rise (200 mm nominal rise).",
  "uncertainty": "Assumed centred 0.9 × 2.1 m connecting doors and south ground-west entrance. Construction is conceptual: junctions, foundations, waterproofing, railings and door swings are undetailed. The 300 mm wall-to-floor gap includes a 200 mm slab. Landing, tread-count and roof/stair headroom need review; no structural, construction, code or accessibility certification.",
